    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="F_abs_simva" name="fraction absorbed simvastatin" value="0.85" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Fraction of simvastatin in the intestinal lumen which is absorbed into
the enterocytes, the rest is excreted in the feces. The absorption of
simvastatin relative to an intravenous dose is about 85 % in two animal
species (Zocor label; 60 - 85 % Cheng1993, Vickers1990a).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="SIMVAABS_k" name="rate of absorption simvastatin" value="1.29" units="per_hr" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>First order rate of the transit of simvastatin from the intestinal
lumen (amount based), split into the absorption (<code>F_abs_simva</code>) and
the fecal excretion of the unabsorbed fraction.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="F_abs_simmets" name="fraction absorbed simvastatin metabolites" value="0.536" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Fraction of the simvastatin metabolites in the intestinal lumen (from
the bile) which is reabsorbed in every round of the enterohepatic
circulation; <code>1 - F_abs_simmets</code> is excreted in the feces. Set with
the renal excretion so that about 13 % of a dose is excreted in the
urine and the rest in the feces (14C simvastatin: 13 % urine, 60 %
feces, Zocor label).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="SIMMETSABS_k" name="rate of absorption simvastatin metabolites" value="0.226" units="per_hr" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>First order rate of the transit of the simvastatin metabolites from
the intestinal lumen (amount based), split into the absorption
(<code>F_abs_simmets</code>) and the fecal excretion.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000322" id="CYP3A4_Km" name="Km CYP3A4" value="0.025" units="mM" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_cyp3a4" name="activity of CYP3A4 (intestine)" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Activity of the intestinal CYP3A4 relative to the reference.
f_cyp3a4 = 1: normal activity;
f_cyp3a4 &lt; 1: reduced activity, inhibition of CYP3A4 (e.g.
grapefruit juice, which inhibits the intestinal CYP3A4 only);
f_cyp3a4 &gt; 1: increased activity, induction of CYP3A4.
Set by the experiments, not fitted.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_cyp3a5" name="functional CYP3A5" value="0" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="r_cyp3a5" name="capacity of CYP3A5 *1/*1 relative to CYP3A4" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000186" id="SIMVA_CYP3A4_Vmax" name="Vmax CYP3A4 simvastatin (intestine)" value="0.0063" units="mmole_per_min_l" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Capacity of the intestinal CYP3A4 for simvastatin, independent of
the liver. Together with <code>SIMVAEXP_Vmax</code> it sets the intestinal
availability (about 0.25 - 0.3, Lilja2004); not identified by the
data of the control arms, not fitted.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000322" id="SIMVAEXP_Km" name="Km simvastatin export" value="0.0097" units="mM" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Assuming the Km of OATP1B1 in the liver for simvastatin lactone
9.7 µM (Chen et al., 2005).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000186" id="SIMVAEXP_Vmax" name="Vmax simvastatin export (intestine)" value="0.001" units="mmole_per_min_l" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000322" id="SIMMETSEXP_Km" name="Km simvastatin metabolite export" value="0.0067" units="mM" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000186" id="SIMMETSEXP_Vmax" name="Vmax simvastatin metabolite export (intestine)" value="0.01" units="mmole_per_min_l" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Export of the reabsorbed metabolites into the gut plasma, fast
compared to their transit (not rate limiting).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
    </listOfParameters>
